#Problem
Given a string s, find the length of the longest substring without duplicate characters.

Example 1:
Input: s = "abcabcbb"
Output: 3

#Intuition

#Approach
1. Define variables int maxLength, char[] chars from the string, Set<Character>
2. Inside for loop define 2 pointers i and j, increment only j
3. Nested while loop while (set.contains(chars[j])) we should remove j element from the set and increment i
4. If set doesn't contain j element - we should add j element to the set and calculate maxLength
5. Return maxLength

#Algorithm

#Complexity
-Time complexity
O(n)

-Space complexity
Auxiliary Space
O(n)

Total Space
O(n)

#Code
class Solution {
    public int lengthOfLongestSubstring(String s) {
        int maxLength = 0;
        char[] chars = s.toCharArray();
        Set<Character> set = new HashSet<>();

        for (int i = 0, j = 0; j < chars.length; j++) {

            while (set.contains(chars[j])) {
                set.remove(chars[i]);
                i++;
            }
            if (!set.contains(chars[j])) {
                set.add(chars[j]);
                maxLength = Math.max(maxLength, set.size());
            }
        }
        return maxLength;
    }
}